queries.answer:
For **TrueNAS API v25.04**, call `filesystem.setacl` with an NFSv4 `dacl` array and set `acltype` to `"NFS4"`. The method runs as a job. ([api.truenas.com](https://api.truenas.com/v25.04.2/api_methods_filesystem.setacl.html?utm_source=openai))

```json
{
  "path": "/mnt/pool/dataset",
  "acltype": "NFS4",
  "dacl": [
    {
      "tag": "owner@",
      "id": -1,
      "type": "ALLOW",
      "perms": { "BASIC": "FULL_CONTROL" },
      "flags": { "BASIC": "INHERIT" }
    },
    {
      "tag": "group@",
      "id": -1,
      "type": "ALLOW",
      "perms": { "BASIC": "MODIFY" },
      "flags": { "BASIC": "INHERIT" }
    },
    {
      "tag": "everyone@",
      "id": -1,
      "type": "ALLOW",
      "perms": { "BASIC": "READ" },
      "flags": { "BASIC": "INHERIT" }
    }
  ],
  "options": {
    "recursive": true,
    "traverse": false,
    "stripacl": false,
    "canonicalize": true,
    "validate_effective_acl": true
  },
  "nfs41_flags": {
    "autoinherit": true,
    "protected": false,
    "defaulted": false
  }
}
```

Key schema points:

- Each NFS4 ACE requires `tag`, `type` (`ALLOW` or `DENY`), `perms`, and `flags`. Valid tags are `owner@`, `group@`, `everyone@`, `USER`, and `GROUP`. Permissions and flags may use their `BASIC` forms—permissions: `FULL_CONTROL`, `MODIFY`, `READ`, or `TRAVERSE`; flags: `INHERIT` or `NOINHERIT`. ([api.truenas.com](https://api.truenas.com/v25.04.2/api_methods_filesystem.setacl.html?utm_source=openai))
- `options.recursive: true` applies the ACL below the target path. If `uid`/`user` or `gid`/`group` is also supplied in a recursive request, TrueNAS changes ownership recursively too. ([api.truenas.com](https://api.truenas.com/v25.04.2/api_methods_filesystem.setacl.html?utm_source=openai))
- For directories, inheritance can also be expressed with advanced flags such as `FILE_INHERIT` and `DIRECTORY_INHERIT`; these control presentation of entries on newly created child objects. ([api.truenas.com](https://api.truenas.com/v25.04.2/api_methods_filesystem.setacl.html?utm_source=openai))
- To avoid guessing the existing ACL shape, retrieve it first with `filesystem.getacl`; its result identifies the ACL format through `acltype` and returns NFS4 ACEs when applicable. ([api.truenas.com](https://api.truenas.com/v25.04.0/api_methods_filesystem.getacl.html?utm_source=openai))

